      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.y
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8545380165161031538, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.z
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogue.sentences.Array.size
      value: 9
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[0]'
      value: Hello Yza... I will livedemo the effects to you. Just check the epic
        code from DialogueTrigger to see how they're done.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[1]'
      value: '[1] Rich Text is <b>bold</b>, <i>italics</i>, <u>underlines</u>, and
        <s>strikethroughs</s>. Done the same as CSS.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[2]'
      value: '[2] Alternating Text Size can change your size, also same as CSS...
        <size=27>A<size=26>A<size=25>A<size=24>A<size=23>A<size=22>A<size=21>A<size=20>A<size=19>A<size=18>A<size=17>A<size=16>A<size=15>A<size=14>A<size=13>A<size=12>A<size=11>A<size=10>A<size=9>A
        <size=36>WOW!'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[3]'
      value: '[3] Coloured Text is again same in CSS. You can go <color=red>L</color><color=orange>G</color><color=yellow>B</color><color=green>T</color><color=blue>Q</color><color=purple>+</color>
        wit dis one.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[4]'
      value: For the CSS stuffs, don't forget that you can combine em!
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[5]'
      value: '[4] Dialogue Shake lets you shake with a <shake> BOOM! sound effect.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[6]'
      value: '[5] Dim is a quick <dim>DUN effect.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[7]'
      value: '[6] Flash is same as dim but with a <flash>DING!'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9041903786073183966, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'dialogue.sentences.Array.data[8]'
      value: Err thas it so far... hmu on Discord for any concerns.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    m_RemovedComponents: []
    m_RemovedGameObjects:
    - {fileID: 9076638287892590626, guid: 09fbf670f6b1442b3895d0264e1b949c, type: 3}
    m_AddedGameObjects: []
